# Docker
*.pid

# Data — anchored to repo root (`/data/`), not `data/`: an unanchored
# pattern matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth, which silently
# swallowed eval/reranker_training/data/ too (git's negation rules can't
# un-ignore a file whose parent directory is excluded — caught by
# `git check-ignore -v` still reporting the file ignored after adding a `!`
# rule for it, not assumed fixed).
/data/

# Unrelated project checkout that happens to live in this directory —
# never part of this repo (it carries its own .git, which is exactly what
# makes an unguarded `git add .` commit it as a broken submodule reference).
/Decision-Support-System-for-Knowledge-Retrieval-RAG-Based-/

# Eval reports are generated per-run and depend on which backend mode
# produced them (real vs. synthetic) — eval/RESULTS.md documents the
# current figures instead of committing raw report dumps.
eval/results/*.json

# Reranker training: the generated training/calibration examples are
# regenerable from eval/reranker_training/generate_training_data.py (same
# precedent as eval/results/*.json above) — dataset_stats.json, the small
# provenance summary, IS committed (needs the explicit `!` below: the
# unanchored "Data" rule above already matches ANY directory named `data`
# at any depth, including this one, so without it dataset_stats.json would
# be silently swallowed along with the regenerable .jsonl files it sits
# next to — caught by checking `git status` after adding this directory,
# not assumed). Model checkpoints are binary weights, never committed —
# training_metadata.json (seed/hyperparameters/dataset stats/timestamp) is
# the real, small, committed reproducibility artifact.
eval/reranker_training/data/*.jsonl
!eval/reranker_training/data/dataset_stats.json
eval/reranker_training/models/finetuned/
eval/reranker_training/models/_trainer_checkpoints/
